          {
            "url": "https://daytonastate.edu/in-the-community/the-arts/index.html",
            "label": "Enjoy the Holidays with Holidazzle: Winter Wonderettes Celebrate the season at Daytona State College's News-Journal Center with a holiday feast, live singers, and Winter Wonderettes, a festive musical featuring '60s holiday classics.Holidazzle Holiday Dinner & Show - 1 Night Only!Friday, December 11 at 6 p.m.Cash Bar AvailableTickets: $50 Adults ($25 Children 12 & Under)Show OnlySaturday, December 12 at 1 p.m.Sunday, December 13 at 2 p.m.Tickets: $10 Adults, $5 Children, $5 Volusia & Flagler County StudentsFree admission for DSC students, faculty, and staff with a valid DSC ID. Get your Holidazzle tickets here."
          },
          {
            "url": "https://daytonastate.edu/news-and-events/news-releases/2026-news-release/national-call-to-action.html",
            "label": "Daytona State College's Commitment to Academic Excellence, Student Opportunity and Public Accountability Daytona State College, founded with innovation at its core and within a culture of continuous improvement, provides opportunities with educational programs that transform students’ lives and communities we serve. We take pride as an outstanding leader in the Florida College System and as a dynamic, nationally recognized institution known for quality, affordable and in-demand programs. Read more."
          },
          {
            "url": "https://daytonastate.edu/academic-departments/college-of-business-engineering-and-technology/school-of-aeronautical-sciences/aerospace-technology-as.html",
            "label": "Enroll now for the Associate of Science degree in Aerospace Technology Daytona State College's Associate of Science in Aerospace Technology degree was developed in collaboration with NASA, Blue Origin, Northrop Grumman and other aerospace industry leaders. Applications are being accepted now. The four-semester program provides hands-on training in aircraft structure fabrication using advanced composite materials, along with instruction in building and testing mechanical systems, wiring and troubleshooting electrical circuits and working with analog and digital devices and electronics assembly. Students will also study industrial safety protocols, quality assurance practices and project management. Learn more here."
          },
          {
            "url": "https://daytonastate.edu/academic-departments/college-of-health-and-public-services/school-of-health-careers/radiologic-and-imaging-sciences-bs-degree.html",
            "label": "New Bachelor of Science degree in Radiologic and Imaging Sciences Enroll now for the new Bachelor of Science in Radiologic and Imaging Sciences (BSRIS) at Daytona State College. This degree expands the professional opportunities available to credentialed imaging technologists. This upper-division program builds upon existing clinical experience and foundational knowledge to prepare imaging professionals for leadership positions and advanced post-primary certification in Computed Tomography (CT). Designed for working radiographers, nuclear medicine technologists, radiation therapists, and sonographers, the BSRIS program provides a flexible, affordable pathway to professional growth. Our students will graduate with the skills to step into supervisory and leadership roles within imaging departments and healthcare organizations. Learn more here."
          },
          {
            "url": "https://daytonastate.edu/on-campus/housing/housing-2nd-phase.html",
            "label": "We Need Your Support! Our first Residence Hall on the Daytona Beach Campus has been a resounding success since opening in Fall 2022. It is home to 256 students, has been at full capacity since its first day of operation, and applications exceed bed space by more than 300%! Students who live on campus are more engaged with instructors, make more use of academic support services, participate in more on-campus activities, connect socially with peers, and build lifelong friendships that help them navigate financial and personal challenges that help them succeed far better in college and in life. To meet this demand, we are embarking on the most ambitious private fundraising endeavor in the College’s history. And we need your help! We’ve set an ambitious goal to raise $16 million to build a second student Residence Hall. Learn more"
          },
